<title>MEXICO: Mexico '96 poultry sector output seen up slightly.</title>
<headline>Mexico '96 poultry sector output seen up slightly.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Output of poultry products -- eggs, chicken and turkey -- are expected to edge up in 1996 to 3.0 million tonnes from 2.9 million last year, a top industry official said on Monday.</p>
<p>Sergio Chavez Gonzalez, director general of the Poultry Farmers Union, said in a telephone interview that production of chicken would be about 1.38 million tonnes and of eggs, about 1.4 million tonnes. He gave no breakdown for turkey.</p>
<p>Last year, he said, there were 1.45 million tonnes of eggs produced, 1.43 million tonnes of chicken and 9,600 tonnes of turkey.</p>
<p>In 1997, he said, poultry farmers expected production to accelerate by four or five percent, chiefly due to an expected recovery in consumption.</p>
<p>-- Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara newsroom +523 817-0397</p>
